# High-Scale PDF Parsing Pipeline: Fatbook Strategy
**Target:** 788MB PDF -> Structured JSON/Markdown -> Neon DB (Next.js)

## 🏗️ Architecture: The "Sidecar" Pattern
Because pure Node.js libraries lack the "Computer Vision" required to parse complex multi-column part tables, we use a Python-based worker (Docling) accessible via a TypeScript SDK.

### 1. Docker Orchestration (`docker-compose.yml`)
Add this to your starter kit to run the parser alongside your Next.js app.

```yaml
services:
  # Your Next.js SaaS App
  web:
    build: .
    ports:
      - "3000:3000"
    environment:
      - PARSER_URL=http://docling-serve:5000

  # The Document Parser (Python Core)
  docling-serve:
    image: quay.io/ds4sd/docling-serve:latest
    ports:
      - "5000:5000"
    deploy:
      resources:
        limits:
          memory: 4gb # Essential for 800MB files